CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal


Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among
hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the
freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs
and products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open
Hardware Licence comes in three variants: this licence, CERN-OHL-S
(which is "Strongly Reciprocal"), and two others, CERN-OHL-W (which is
"Weakly Reciprocal") and CERN-OHL-P (which is "Permissive"). Their
key difference is the extent of "copyleft": CERN-OHL-P doesn't require
derivative works to be licensed under the same terms; CERN-OHL-W
requires that derivative Works on the HDL (hardware description
language) level are licensed under CERN-OHL-W; CERN-OHL-S requires
that all derivative Works and all Products are licensed under
CERN-OHL-S.

                       CERN-OHL-S Version 2
              Copyright CERN 2020.
              CERN-OHL-S Version 2 was released in 2020.

            How to use this Licence

To apply this Licence to a specific Source, use the following
boilerplate notice:

  Copyright [year] [name of Licensor]

  This source describes Open Hardware and is licensed under the
  CERN-OHL-S v2.

  You may redistribute and modify this source and make products
  using it under the terms of the CERN-OHL-S v2
  (https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt).

  This source is distributed WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED
  WARRANTY, INCLUDING OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY
  AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. Please see the CERN-OHL-S
  v2 for applicable conditions.

  Source location: [URL where the source is hosted]

  As per CERN-OHL-S v2 section 4, should You produce hardware
  based on this source, You must where practicable maintain the
  Source Location visible on the external case of any product you
  make using this source.

          1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S v2.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

       a) any version of the CERN-OHL-S

       b) a licence which permits the recipients of the work to
          which it applies to use, modify, create Derivatives of,
          distribute and sublicense Contributions and Derivatives
          of those Contributions, requiring that all such
          Contributions and Derivatives are made available under
          this Compatible Licence.

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or
      digital code which can be applied to Make or test a Product
      or to prepare a Product for use, Conveyance or sale,
      regardless of its medium or how it is expressed. It may
      include Notices.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made
      available under this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical
      object, whether in finished or intermediate form, arising
      from the use, application or processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by
      manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying
      Covered Source or another Product or otherwise.

  1.7 'Available Component' means any part, subsystem, module or
      device component other than Covered Source available under a
      Compatible Licence from which a Product can be Made.

  1.8 'External Material' means anything other than Covered Source
      and a Product made by applying it, and includes but is not
      limited to:
        a) any driver software, firmware or middleware required to
           make a Product function;
        b) any tool required for the design, manufacture or testing
           of a Product;
        c) written documentation, including but not limited to
           bills of materials, assembly instructions, operating
           instructions and maintenance documentation.

  1.9 'Publicly Available' means that copies are available for
      anyone to obtain, free of charge, by accessing a URI, and
      that copies remain publicly available at that URI for at
      least as long as the Product or Source is available to be
      Made or purchased.

  1.10 'Derivative' means anything derived by modification of or
       from Covered Source, including:
         a) any work derived from it by translation, adaptation,
            selection or arrangement;
         b) any modification of the Source itself.

  1.11 'Contribution' means a Derivative of the Covered Source
       which is made available under this Licence.

  1.12 'Contributor' means a person or legal entity who makes a
       Contribution.

  1.13 'Licensor' means a person or legal entity who creates or
       modifies Covered Source. A person or legal entity can be
       both a Licensor and a Contributor.

  1.14 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark
       notices, references to the Licence, disclaimer of
       warranties, and all notices that refer to the Licence and
       to the disclaimer of warranties that are included in the
       Covered Source.

  1.15 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person or legal entity
       exercising rights under this Licence.

  1.16 'Convey' means to communicate, publish, distribute,
       disseminate, transfer or make available by any means,
       including but not limited to sale.

          2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification,
      Conveyance of Covered Source and Products, and the Making of
      Products. By exercising any right granted under this
      Licence, You irrevocably accept these terms and conditions.

  2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You,
      and shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.

  2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise
      the rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.

  2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair
      dealing, or any other similar right.

          3 Copying, Modifying and Conveying Covered Source

  3.1 You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of the Covered
      Source, in any medium, provided You retain all Notices.

  3.2 You may modify the Covered Source, other than Notices,
      provided that You irrevocably undertake to make that
      modified Source available in the same way as the original
      Covered Source within thirty (30) days of the date when
      You first Convey it, and that You add a Notice to the
      modified Source stating that You have modified it, with the
      date and brief description of how You have modified it.

  3.3 You may Convey modified Covered Source (with the effect
      that You will also become a Licensor) provided that You:

       a) retain Notices as required in subsection 3.2;

       b) add a Notice to the Covered Source stating that You
          have modified it, with the date and brief description
          of how You have modified it;

       c) add a Notice to the modified Covered Source prominently
          stating that it is available under this Licence, with
          the text of, or the Uniform Resource Identifier (URI)
          for, this Licence; and

       d) make the Source available under the same or a
          Compatible Licence.

  3.4 You may Convey Covered Source with additional terms
      provided that:

       a) those terms are not intended to and do not restrict the
          recipient's rights under this Licence;

       b) those terms are compatible with the terms of this
          Licence;

       c) if the additional terms are clearly identified as being
          separate from this Licence, the recipient may exercise
          their rights under this Licence without reference to
          the additional terms.

  3.5 If You are a Contributor, You grant the Licensor a
      non-exclusive, irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide, royalty-
      free licence to use and sublicense under any licence the
      Contributions You make.

  3.6 Whilst every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy
      and quality of this Licence, the Licensor and CERN make no
      warranties in respect of it. Nothing in this Licence
      constitutes legal advice. This Licence has been prepared
      and is provided on the basis that it adequately serves the
      purpose for which it is intended. CERN recommends that, in
      the event of any legal uncertainty, legal advice is obtained.

          4 Making and Conveying Products

You may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided that You
ensure that the recipient of the Product has access, in the way
described in subsection 4.1, to the Covered Source and any
Notice for the Product.

  4.1 The Covered Source may be:

       a) Packaged with the Product in physical or digital form;

       b) offered to the recipient, and retained by You, for a
          period of at least 3 years from the date You first
          Convey the Product. Such an offer shall be valid for
          any recipient of the Product, and shall entitle them
          to receive, within thirty (30) days of their written
          request to You, a copy of the Covered Source on a
          physical or digital medium. You shall not charge any
          fee for the copy or its Conveyance; or

       c) accompanied by a written offer, valid for at least
          three years from the date You first Convey the Product,
          to provide anyone who requests it with a copy of the
          Covered Source. If You offer (b) or (c), the copy of
          the Covered Source shall also include a copy of the
          Notices for the Product.

  4.2 Where You Convey a Product You must ensure that any
      Notice on the outside of the Product or its packaging
      states that it has been made from Source licensed under
      the CERN-OHL-S, that You have applied modifications to the
      Source and (if desired) how it can be obtained. Notices on
      the outside of the Product and/or on its packaging shall
      also include the Source Location as required by
      subsection 3.3(d) and shall not be modified. You must
      include a copy of the Notices with the Product.

          5 Research and Personal Use

Notwithstanding the above, You may copy and Modify the Covered
Source for research and non-commercial personal use only,
provided that You add a Notice to the modified Source. You may
not Convey such modified Source to others. Publishing your
modifications in a journal or similar does not constitute
Conveying.

